and let \(\langle\cdot,\cdot\rangle\) denote the duality between \(\Theta_{h}\) and its dual \(\Theta_{h}^{\prime}\) for the \(L^{2}\)-norm. Then

\[c(\phi,\mu_{h})=\langle C_{h}(\phi),\mu_{h}\rangle\]

where \(C_{h}\in\mathcal{L}(W^{k+1,\,p}(\Omega)\cap H^{1}_{0}(\Omega);\Theta_{h}^{ \prime})\) for all integers \(k\in[1,l]\) and

\[\|\,C_{h}\|_{\mathcal{L}(W^{k+1,\,p}(\Omega)\cap H^{1}_{0}(\Omega);\Theta_{h} )}\leqslant Ch^{k-1/2-1/p}.\]

Therefore by interpolating between two consecutive integral values of \(k\), we derive from Theorem I.1.4 that \(C_{h}\in\mathcal{L}(W^{k+1,\,p}(\Omega)\cap H^{1}_{0}(\Omega);\Theta_{h}^{ \prime})\) for all \(real\,k\in[1,l]\) and formula (I.1.10) permits to extend (3.3) to non integral \(k\):

\[\sup_{\mu_{h}\in\Theta_{h}}\frac{|(\operatorname{\mathbf{curl}}(\phi-\hat{P_{ h}}\phi),\operatorname{\mathbf{curl}}\mu_{h})|}{\|\,\mu_{h}\|_{0,\Omega}} \leqslant Ch^{k-1/2-1/p}\|\,\phi\|_{k+1,\,p,\Omega}\quad\quad\forall\text{real }k\in[1,l].\] (3.5)

With these two lemmas, we are able to improve the approximation result in \(V_{h}\).

**Lemma 3.3**.: _Assume that \(\Omega\) and \(\mathcal{T}_{h}\) are like in Lemma 3.2. For each real \(k\in[1,l]\) and real \(p\in[2,\,\infty],\) there exists a constant \(C>0,\) independent of \(h,\) such that all functions \(v=(\operatorname{\mathbf{curl}}\phi,\theta=-\,\Delta\phi)\in\widetilde{V}\) with \(\phi\in W^{k+1,\,p}(\Omega)\cap H^{1}_{0}(\Omega)\) satisfy:_

\[\left\{\begin{aligned} \inf_{w_{h}\in V_{h}}|v-w_{h}|& \leqslant 2\inf_{\theta_{h}\in\Theta_{h}}\|\theta-\theta_{h}\|_{0, \Omega}+Ch^{k-1/2-1/p}\|\,\phi\|_{k+1,\,p,\Omega},\\ \inf_{w_{h}\in V_{h}}\|\,v-w_{h}\|_{\widetilde{x}}& \leqslant 2\left\{|\phi-\hat{P_{h}}\phi|_{1,s,\Omega}+\inf_{\theta_{h} \in\Theta_{h}}\|\theta-\theta_{h}\|_{0,\Omega}\right\}\\ &\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad+Ch^{k-1/2-1/p}\|\,\phi \|_{k+1,\,p,\Omega}.\end{aligned}\right.\] (3.6)

_When \(\phi\in H^{l\pm 3/2}(\Omega)\cap W^{l+1,\,\infty}(\Omega)\) (and of course \(\phi|_{\,\Gamma}=0\)), the best estimate is:_

